# MAP DRIVES [
# format:
# <from> <local> [alias] #
# if local == 0 then disable

"/Volumes/1T" "~/media/1T" 1T
"/mnt/c" 0 
"test0/t0" "test0-t0" t0

# MAP DRIVES ]
# ---- INFO ---- [

Configuration options for the SETTINGS JSON section.

Database backend.

Supported values:

    "db": "memory"   # In-memory database (fastest, not persistent)
    "db": "sqlite"   # SQLite database stored on disk
    "db": "redis"    # Redis database (todo)

# ---- INFO ---- ]
# SETTINGS JSON [
{
    "db": "sqlite",
    "db_fragments": {}
}
# SETTINGS JSON ]

# Path fragments: add catalog prefixes (after MAP DRIVES alias translation) to
# db_fragments, for example {"/1T": "fragments/1T.sqlite"}. Relative database
# filenames resolve from the launch directory. Activate new paths explicitly:
# ./run.sh -refragment
# Migration is lazy when browsing directories or writing files. Nested paths use
# the longest matching prefix; unassigned data stays in drivevfs.
# Export to a new/empty directory: ./run.sh -export-livelog /tmp/catalog-export
